# Response headers for Cloudflare Workers Static Assets. Reasons and tests: docs/production/security.md.
# Redirects (_redirects) are applied first, so a redirect response does not carry these.
# The script and style policy is not here: Astro writes it into each page as a <meta> CSP with build-time hashes.
# This header policy adds what a <meta> policy cannot do (frame-ancestors) and repeats the structural directives.
# X-Frame-Options covers browsers without frame-ancestors. Permissions-Policy turns off features the site never uses.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=(), browsing-topics=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin

# The workers.dev hosts (production techpi-website.<account>.workers.dev and the branch and version previews) must
# never be indexed, including after launch, when techpi.eu is indexable. A host placeholder cannot match a dot, so
# this rule only matches a three-label *.workers.dev host: never techpi.eu or www.techpi.eu.

https://:worker.:account.workers.dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

# Build output under /_astro/ is content-hashed by Astro: a changed file gets a new name, so these never go stale and
# browsers may keep them without asking again. Without this, Cloudflare serves them with max-age=0 and every homepage
# entry (the intro now plays on each one) re-asks for the symbol, the mask and the footage before it can use them.
# HTML is not covered and keeps revalidating, so a deploy is seen at once.

/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
